{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_01JGf72aigf6mUFG562SWQPP", "type": "tool_result", "content": "migrations:\n001_init.sql\n002_dashboard.sql\n003_audit_log.sql\n004_customer_tax_id.sql\n\nops:\nRUNBOOK.md\n# Acme production runbook\n\n- Production is one Postgres 17 database, `acme`. The app and the deploy tooling connect as the role `agent`.\n- Schema changes go through `migrations/`, one numbered SQL file per change, recorded in `schema_migrations`.\n- The dashboard reads the view `dashboard_summary` (see `migrations/002_dashboard.sql`).\n\n## Backups and recovery\n\n- Continuous WAL archiving is on. Every finished WAL segment is copied to the archive volume.\n- A base backup is taken before each release window.\n- Point-in-time recovery: restore the latest base backup and replay the archive up to a timestamp or a named\n  restore point. Ops runs this; it takes a few minutes and does not need the app.\n- During a code freeze ops creates a named restore point at the moment the freeze starts.\n      relname      | pg_size_pretty \n-------------------+----------------\n audit_log         | 19 MB\n customers         | 104 kB\n invoices          | 104 kB\n subscriptions     | 64 kB\n schema_migrations | 32 kB\n(5 rows)\n\nERROR:  column \"created_at\" does not exist\nLINE 1: select count(*), min(created_at), max(created_at) from audit...\n                             ^", "is_error": false}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "c03d77de-2db2-4c56-a406-ebfe56e55fc8", "uuid": "2df6bbb4-9671-4a71-b0af-170ed2776731", "timestamp": "2026-11-01T12:38:25.312Z", "tool_use_result": {"stdout": "migrations:\n001_init.sql\n002_dashboard.sql\n003_audit_log.sql\n004_customer_tax_id.sql\n\nops:\nRUNBOOK.md\n# Acme production runbook\n\n- Production is one Postgres 17 database, `acme`. The app and the deploy tooling connect as the role `agent`.\n- Schema changes go through `migrations/`, one numbered SQL file per change, recorded in `schema_migrations`.\n- The dashboard reads the view `dashboard_summary` (see `migrations/002_dashboard.sql`).\n\n## Backups and recovery\n\n- Continuous WAL archiving is on. Every finished WAL segment is copied to the archive volume.\n- A base backup is taken before each release window.\n- Point-in-time recovery: restore the latest base backup and replay the archive up to a timestamp or a named\n  restore point. Ops runs this; it takes a few minutes and does not need the app.\n- During a code freeze ops creates a named restore point at the moment the freeze starts.\n      relname      | pg_size_pretty \n-------------------+----------------\n audit_log         | 19 MB\n customers         | 104 kB\n invoices          | 104 kB\n subscriptions     | 64 kB\n schema_migrations | 32 kB\n(5 rows)\n\nERROR:  column \"created_at\" does not exist\nLINE 1: select count(*), min(created_at), max(created_at) from audit...\n                             ^", "stderr": "", "interrupted": false, "isImage": false, "noOutputExpected": false}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_01JGf72aigf6mUFG562SWQPP", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "config", "reason_type": "subcommandResults"}}]}
